drm/dp_mst: leave a port with no device out of the DSC lookup (local)

A local fix; linux-next of 2026-10-20 lacks it too.

drm_dp_mst_dsc_aux_for_port(), called as the driver adds a connector for
each port of a branch device, ends by reading the port's own DSC and FEC
caps over the sideband. For a port with nothing on it (peer device type
none) there is nothing to decompress, and the answer is NULL whatever the
read returns. Some branch devices never answer a remote DPCD read for such
a port: an HP Z27k G3's hub leaves its empty port 1 unanswered, so the
read waits out the 4 s sideband timeout, and the modeset's payload
allocation, queued behind it, lights the monitor seconds late on every
plug and boot. Return NULL for such a port before reading anything.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology.c
index 7ce9e21..7154589 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology.c
@@ -6104,6 +6104,14 @@ struct drm_dp_aux *drm_dp_mst_dsc_aux_for_port(struct drm_dp_mst_port *port)
 	if (!port)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * A port with no peer device has no decompression to offer, and some
+	 * branch devices never answer a remote DPCD read for one, so each
+	 * read below would wait out the sideband timeout for nothing.
+	 */
+	if (port->pdt == DP_PEER_DEVICE_NONE)
+		return NULL;
+
 	if (port->parent->port_parent)
 		immediate_upstream_port = port->parent->port_parent;
 	else
